{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**Tracking error** is the standard deviation of daily fund-minus-benchmark total returns over the agreed one-year period, annualized only under the agreed convention. **Cumulative tracking difference** is the difference between their compounded period returns.\n\nIf tracking error exceeds the mandate’s expected range, investigate:\n\n- **Portfolio:** sampling/optimization deviations, concentration constraints, cash balances, dividend-reinvestment timing, futures exposure, index-rebalance timing, corporate actions, trading costs and securities-lending effects.\n- **Pricing/data:** mismatched valuation times, stale or fair-valued prices, incorrect holdings/prices, dividend adjustments, benchmark versions and total-return conventions. Establish whether fund returns use NAV or market prices; premiums/discounts and bid–ask effects can distort market-price comparisons.\n- **Operations:** creation/redemption cash flows, settlement failures, missed trades, reconciliation breaks, dividend accruals, fee accrual errors and index/data implementation errors.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Stable expense drag primarily affects tracking difference; variable implementation effects drive tracking error. No single cause should be presumed."}}
